# Force LF in the repository for every text file.
#
# Why this matters here: on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for
# Windows default), a fresh clone rewrites every LF to CRLF. These source files
# contain non-ASCII text in comments, and the vitest/esbuild transform step
# fails with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" on the CRLF form while
# the LF form parses fine — the same commit, the same toolchain, only the line
# endings differ. Verified by cloning this repo and running the suite.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out as LF regardless of
# the user's autocrlf setting, so the clone matches what the tests were written
# against.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
